[{"_1":2},"llms/mdx",{"_3":4},"data","# Capabilities (/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities)\n\n\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  `GET /updates/v1/capabilities` tells a client which backend is active (`native` or `hawkbit`) and which of 22 features it supports. Read it once and hide what does not apply. An operation the backend does not implement answers **`501 Not Implemented`**, never `500`; a `501` is a permanent property of the deployment, so retrying will not help. The one exception is `GET /workflows`, which answers an empty list in hawkBit mode.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Read the capabilities [#read-the-capabilities]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  The route takes no parameters and has no side effects. The service serves it without authentication, like `/health`; a gateway in front of it may still require a token.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  ```bash\n  curl -s https://lamassu.example.com/api/updates/v1/capabilities \\\n    -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"\n  ```\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  The response has three fields:\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Field         | Type             | Meaning                                                                                                                   |\n  | ------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n  | `backend`     | string           | `native` or `hawkbit`                                                                                                     |\n  | `supported`   | object           | One boolean per flag. It always carries all 22 keys, so a missing key means a client/server version skew, not \"supported\" |\n  | `unsupported` | array of strings | The flags that are `false`, repeated for convenience, in the order of the table below                                     |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  An example for a native deployment:\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"backend\": \"native\",\n    \"supported\": {\n      \"latest_versions\": true,\n      \"version_compliance\": true,\n      \"artifact_signatures\": true,\n      \"artifact_encryption\": true,\n      \"per_device_encryption\": true,\n      \"artifact_download_by_name\": true,\n      \"workflows\": true,\n      \"launch_strategy_update\": true,\n      \"launch_complete\": true,\n      \"launch_device_assignment\": true,\n      \"scheduled_launch\": true,\n      \"push_events\": true,\n      \"launch_preconditions\": true,\n      \"campaigns\": true,\n      \"canary_device\": true,\n      \"device_inventory\": true,\n      \"artifact_catalog\": true,\n      \"prebuilt_deliverable\": true,\n      \"software_module_composition\": true,\n      \"software_module_deliverables\": false,\n      \"standalone_software_modules\": true,\n      \"software_module_replace\": false\n    },\n    \"unsupported\": [\"software_module_deliverables\", \"software_module_replace\"]\n  }\n  ```\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Per-backend support [#per-backend-support]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  \"Yes\" means supported. \"Conditional\" means it depends on configuration or on the hawkBit server; see the notes after the table.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  | Capability                                                                                                  | native                  | hawkbit                       |\n  | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n  | `latest_versions`: declare the latest version per group, plus per-device drift and force-sync               | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `version_compliance`: group-wide compliance and version-status reports                                      | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `artifact_signatures`: signed version manifests and the artifacts archive                                   | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `artifact_encryption`: shared-key encryption and KMS signing at build                                       | Yes                     | Conditional                   |\n  | `per_device_encryption`: one deliverable per device, each with its own key                                  | Yes                     | **No**                        |\n  | `artifact_download_by_name`: fetch a pack's staged file by file name                                        | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `workflows`: choose the WFX workflow per launch                                                             | Yes                     | **No**                        |\n  | `launch_strategy_update`: edit the strategy after creation                                                  | Yes                     | **No**                        |\n  | `launch_complete`: mark a launch complete early                                                             | Yes                     | **No**                        |\n  | `launch_device_assignment`: add devices to a launch after creation (a service operation with no HTTP route) | Yes                     | **No**                        |\n  | `scheduled_launch`: start a launch at a future time                                                         | Yes (the service polls) | Yes (hawkBit's own scheduler) |\n  | `push_events`: server-pushed job state                                                                      | Yes                     | **No** (poll)                 |\n  | `launch_preconditions`: gate the deployable devices on installed versions                                   | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `campaigns`: plan, start, pause, resume, cancel, retry failed                                               | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `canary_device`: the first batch is one named device                                                        | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `device_inventory`: which pack version a device carries, and its update history                             | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `artifact_catalog`: fleet-wide artifact catalog and per-pack listing                                        | Yes                     | Yes                           |\n  | `prebuilt_deliverable`: attach an externally built file to a pack                                           | Yes                     | **No**                        |\n  | `software_module_composition`: a pack is a composition of typed modules                                     | Yes                     | Conditional                   |\n  | `software_module_deliverables`: each module has its own deliverable                                         | **No**                  | Yes                           |\n  | `standalone_software_modules`: create a module with no pack                                                 | Yes                     | Conditional                   |\n  | `software_module_replace`: swap a module for another version of itself                                      | **No**                  | Conditional                   |\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Conditional flags in hawkBit mode [#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  * **`artifact_encryption`** is reported unsupported only when none of `swugenerator_path`, `symkms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` is configured. Each build option still needs its own settings: see [Signing and encryption](/docs/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption).\n  * **`software_module_composition`, `standalone_software_modules` and `software_module_replace`** depend on the hawkBit server having the pre-seeded `os` and `application` module types and the `os_app` or `app` set type. The service probes this with a 5 second timeout, caches the result for about five minutes and assumes support when hawkBit is unreachable. When the probe fails, all three flags are reported unsupported together.\n  * **`software_module_deliverables`** is always reported supported in hawkBit mode. Building a `swu-build` module still needs a `swugenerator_path`, and without one the build answers `501`.\n  * **`prebuilt_deliverable`**: a hawkBit pack is never built directly. A `swu-prebuilt` catalog module accepts a finished `.swu` instead.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Flags that differ in meaning [#flags-that-differ-in-meaning]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Both backends report `software_module_composition`, but importing a module **links** it in hawkBit mode (both packs share one module) and **copies** it in native mode. The reusable-modules list reports this per candidate in its `shared` field, so a client can tell the operator which one they get. See [Concepts](/docs/platform/updates/concepts).\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  In native mode a launch dispatches one job per device with a single download URI, so a module has no deliverable of its own: the pack builds one `.swu` from every module's inputs. That is why `software_module_deliverables` and `software_module_replace` are unsupported there.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  What a client should do [#what-a-client-should-do]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  * Call `capabilities` once at start-up and before showing a feature the table marks as backend-dependent.\n  * Treat a `501` on a route as authoritative: hide the action instead of retrying.\n  * Do not infer the backend from the URL. Both serve the same `/updates/v1` routes; see the [API reference](/docs/platform/updates/reference/api) for which routes answer `501` in which backend.\n  * Re-read the capabilities after changing hawkBit's module types or the build configuration.\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  Next steps [#next-steps]\n</div>\n\n<div className=\"lm-diff-ins lm-diff-block\">\n  * [API reference](/docs/platform/updates/reference/api)\n  * [hawkBit mode](/docs/platform/updates/hawkbit-mode)\n</div>\n"]
